rp2040: a DMA channel allocation that does not wait

Purpose: rp2040_dmachannel() waits on the channel counting semaphore until
a channel is free, for ever when other users keep all twelve.  The I2C0
DMA reads of the board (common/drivers/i2c_dw/port/nuttx/
i2c_dw_dma_os_rp2040.c) take two channels at the start of I2C0; with one
channel free or none, that start would wait and I2C0 would never come up,
where it should go on without the DMA and read on the interrupts.

- arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_dmac.c, rp2040_dmac.h:
  rp2040_dmachannel_trywait(), which never waits.  It takes the count with
  nxsem_trywait() and returns NULL at once when no channel is free; it
  takes the allocator's lock with nxmutex_trylock() and, when another task
  holds it (a channel is being allocated or freed), gives the count back
  and returns NULL, so no channel is lost.  A caller may try again.
  Otherwise it does what rp2040_dmachannel() does (the lowest free
  channel, its flag cleared and its interrupt enabled).
  rp2040_dmachannel() is unchanged.

Zephyr: Zephyr's dma_request_channel() (include/zephyr/drivers/dma.h)
does not wait either; it returns an error when no channel is free.

diff --git a/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_dmac.c b/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_dmac.c
index d4914dcb..235e287e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_dmac.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_dmac.c
@@ -262,6 +262,78 @@ DMA_HANDLE rp2040_dmachannel(void)
   return (DMA_HANDLE)dmach;
 }
 
+/****************************************************************************
+ * Name: rp2040_dmachannel_trywait
+ *
+ * Description:
+ *   Allocate a DMA channel without waiting at any point.  As
+ *   rp2040_dmachannel(), but it returns NULL at once when no DMA channel is
+ *   free or when another task holds the allocator's lock (a channel is
+ *   being allocated or freed); the semaphore count it took is then given
+ *   back, so no channel is lost.  A caller may try again.
+ *
+ * Input parameters:
+ *   None
+ *
+ * Returned Value:
+ *   A DMA channel handle, or NULL if no channel is free or the allocator
+ *   is busy.
+ *
+ ****************************************************************************/
+
+DMA_HANDLE rp2040_dmachannel_trywait(void)
+{
+  struct dma_channel_s *dmach;
+  unsigned int ch;
+  uint32_t bit = 0;
+  int ret;
+
+  /* Take a count from the channel counting semaphore if there is one,
+   * without waiting.  When we get the count, then we can be assured that a
+   * channel is available in the channel list and is reserved for us.
+   */
+
+  ret = nxsem_trywait(&g_dmac.chansem);
+  if (ret < 0)
+    {
+      return NULL;
+    }
+
+  /* Get exclusive access to the DMA channel list without waiting.  If
+   * another task holds it, give the count back and return NULL.
+   */
+
+  ret = nxmutex_trylock(&g_dmac.lock);
+  if (ret < 0)
+    {
+      nxsem_post(&g_dmac.chansem);
+      return NULL;
+    }
+
+  /* Search for an available DMA channel */
+
+  for (ch = 0, dmach = NULL; ch < RP2040_DMA_NCHANNELS; ch++)
+    {
+      struct dma_channel_s *candidate = &g_dmach[ch];
+      if (!candidate->inuse)
+        {
+          dmach        = candidate;
+          dmach->inuse = true;
+
+          bit = 1 << ch;
+          break;
+        }
+    }
+
+  nxmutex_unlock(&g_dmac.lock);
+
+  setbits_reg32(bit, RP2040_DMA_INTS0);
+  setbits_reg32(bit, RP2040_DMA_INTE0);
+
+  DEBUGASSERT(dmach);
+  return (DMA_HANDLE)dmach;
+}
+
